    "# Graph Digital Twin for Smart Grid Cyber-Resilience\n",
    "### Detecting and Localizing False Data Injection Attacks (FDIAs) on the IEEE 14-Bus System\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements a topology-aware **Graph Digital Twin** designed to detect and localize stealthy False Data Injection Attacks (FDIAs).\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Project Architecture:\n",
    "1. **Grid Simulation (pandapower):** Simulates grid operating states under random load variations and programmatically injects local stealthy attacks.\n",
    "2. **Multi-Task GraphSAGE Network:** Performs simultaneous attack detection (graph classification) and localization (node classification).\n",
    "3. **Explainable AI (Integrated Gradients):** Computes feature attribution weights to identify exactly which physical measurements (e.g., voltage angle) at which buses were manipulated.\n",
    "4. **Model Comparison:** Benchmarks the proposed topology-invariant GraphSAGE against traditional MLP (Flat), GCN, and GAT models.\n",
    "\n",
