   "source": [
    "## Section 2: Multi-Task GNN Architecture & Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "We define and compare four different machine learning models:\n",
    "1. **Traditional MLP (Flat):** Treats the grid measurements as a flat vector, completely ignoring the physical network connections.\n",
    "2. **GCN (Isotropic Graph Conv):** Message passing averages neighboring features uniformly.\n",
    "3. **GAT (Attention Graph Conv):** Message passing weights neighbors dynamically using self-attention.\n",
    "4. **GraphSAGE (Proposed Graph Conv):** Learnable neighborhood aggregation.\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Academic Novelty\n",
    "While Flat MLP achieves high accuracy on static grids, it lacks **topology-invariance** (cannot handle dynamic changes like line outages or expansions). GNNs learn local interaction rules, allowing them to generalise to any grid layout without retraining."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
